otBefore="1210-01-01" notAfter="1210-12-31">1210</birth><death notBefore="1285-12-11" notAfter="1285-12-11">1285-12-11</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1060</idno><idno type="APIS">3977</idno><note type="comment">Seventh abbot of sNar thang monastery (ID:4411). On his dates see [2X2E3882]: 260, n. 146.</note></person><person xml:id="person4006"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རིགས་པའི་རལ་གྲི</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rig pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs ral</persName><birth notBefore="1227-01-01" notAfter="1227-12-31">1227</birth><death notBefore="1305-08-29" notAfter="1305-08-29">1305-08-29</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1217</idno><idno type="APIS">4006</idno><note type="comment">On his career, see [KHA9ZVGP]: 3-8.&#13;
The dates 1227-1305 are known from the biography (see work (ID:7016)) composed by his student bSam gtan bzang po (ID:4005) ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).&#13;
His name in religion was Dar ma rgyal mtshan or Chos kyi rgyal mtshan ([FZ6N88AU]: 406) - the name Chos kyi rgyal mtshan is given as his "real name" (mtshan dngos) in a homage by Rong ston ([KM47ZZDJ]: 657 and n. 62). &#13;
The majority of the colophons of his works name him "bCom ldan ral gri," a few "Rigs/Rig pa’i ral gri" or just "Ral gri." Schwabland's discussion of the variants “Rigs pa” and “Rig pa” does not come to a definite conclusion as to which is the correct spelling ([CTQMVBPR]: 2-3).&#13;
He was born as the son of a local wealthy headman, the fourth of five sons and his birth is reported to have been foretold by Śākyaśrībhadra (ID:6418) when he was invited by Ral gri's paternal uncle ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).</note></person><person xml:id="person4025"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang drug pa rdo rje 'od zer</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཙང་དྲུག་པ་རྡོ་རྗེ་འོད་ཟེར</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang drug rdo rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang drug pa rdo rje 'od zer</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang pa drug po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang pa gru gu</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang drug</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nyi ma sbral nag gtsang pa drug po</persName><birth notBefore="1150-01-01" notAfter="1200-12-31">after 1150 before 1200</birth><death notBefore="1210-01-01" notAfter="1250-12-31">after 1210 before 1250</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3JT13459</idno><idno type="APIS">4025</idno><note type="comment">Argued to be identical with  gNyal zhig's student gTsang pa gru gu in [4LWBNM7B]: 119-120.&#13;
