a</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">A fragmentary manuscript of the Tibetan translation (different from the canonical one) from Matho is discussed in [5H5BVSWI].</note><idno type="APIS">3727</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work3774"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">pramāṇaviniścaya</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam par nges pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam nges</title><date type="composition" notBefore="0560-01-01" notAfter="0660-12-31">after 560 before 660</date><author ref="person:3773">dharmakīrti</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">3774</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5002"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gcod kyi gdams pa nam mkha' sgo 'byed</title><title xml:lang="bo">གཅོད་ཀྱི་གདམས་པ་ནམ་མཁའ་སྒོ་འབྱེད</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1237-01-01">after 1237</date><author ref="person:4006">rigs pa'i ral gri</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Teaching given by Ral gri (ID:4006) to sKyi ston grags pa rgyal mtshan (ID:4221).</note><idno type="APIS">5002</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5149"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa'i spyod pa la 'jug pa'i rgyan</title><title xml:lang="bo">བྱང་ཆུབ་སེམས་དཔའི་སྤྱོད་པ་ལ་འཇུག་པའི་རྒྱན</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bo d+hi sa t+wa tsar+ya ba ta ra a lang ka ra</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1210-01-01" notAfter="1299-12-31">after 1210 before 1299</date><author ref="person:4221">skyi ston grags pa rgyal mtshan</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The author is well versed in the tools of scholasticism and presents the materials by way of proofs and arguments by consequence.&#13;
